A||N||4||Iceman||Fiero Option Codes||||1||
Z||000000||Iceman||12-27-2000||09:18 PM||||I am a little confused about some of the option codes on my 85 GT any help would be greatly appreciated.<P>1)What exactly is Beauville/STX Rally Equipment?<BR>2)What is the WS6 special performance package?<BR>3)Does any one know what the following codes are?<BR>D84,D4T,E52,P84,PDN,YT9,139,16L.  All are found on the Option code decal on the LF wheel well.<BR>4)Does any one have any info on the factory spring rates for spring codes: FJH & NYM||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||12-27-2000||10:54 PM||||1)What exactly is Beauville/STX Rally Equipment?<P>Beats me.<P>2)What is the WS6 special performance package?<P>Springs, shocks and swapbar. Considered "sport" and usually requires a kidney belt. Typically the hardest ride available. <P>3)Does any one know what the following codes are?<BR>D84 - Two Tone Paint<BR>D4T - Likely a speedo gear, but not listed. E52 - Wrap around doors on a Toronado!<BR>P84 - Tires, but not listed.<BR>PDN - Wheels or wheel cover, but not listed.<BR>YT9 - Chime, but not listed.<BR>139 - Interior trim - Lt Slate Grey<BR>16L - Secondary Interior Color Warm Grey Metallic.<P><BR>4)Does any one have any info on the factory spring rates for spring codes: FJH & NYM<P>FJH - WS6 Front Spring, Highest Load Rate.<BR>NYM - WS6 Rear Spring, Highest Load Rate.<P>Maybe someone can fill in the blanks.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ronnie||12-27-2000||11:56 PM||||The Beauville and STX Rally , are codes for Chevrolet vans||||reg||6
Z||000003||terryk||12-28-2000||12:13 AM||||Ah ha, so there was a Fiero Van.....<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||baldlobo||12-28-2000||03:06 AM||||<BR>D84,D4T,E52,P84,PDN,YT9,139,16L<P>E52	DOOR REAR, 83 INCH, WRAP AROUND<BR>YT9	FISHER FURNISHED PARTS||||reg||1
